course: dictionary
lesson: 14074
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Mayo can mean a creamy sauce, or it can be the name of a place in Ireland. Look at the words around it to see which meaning the writer wants. Those words are its context.
explain: «I'd like a chicken sandwich with mayo, please.» The words chicken, sandwich and please are clues. You spread mayo on food, so here mayo means the sauce.
explain: «We drove along the wild coast of Mayo, past the mountains.» The words coast and mountains are clues. A coast and mountains belong to a place, so here Mayo is a county in Ireland.
fact: Mayo is short for mayonnaise, a thick, creamy white sauce.
fact: Mayonnaise is made from egg yolks, oil, and lemon juice or vinegar.
fact: Mayo is a noun you cannot count: you say some mayo, not two mayos.
fact: Mayo is also a county in the west of Ireland, known for its coast, mountains and Gaelic football.
fact: Mayonnaise with raw egg should be kept cold, in the fridge.
exercise: «I'd like chips with mayo, please.» What does mayo mean here? | A green vegetable | A county in Ireland | *A creamy sauce | A type of bread
exercise: «We drove along the wild coast of Mayo.» What does Mayo mean here? | *A county in the west of Ireland | A creamy sauce | A kind of sandwich | A large shop
exercise: «The shop sells ham, cheese and mayo.» Find one word that tells you mayo is a food. | county | *ham | sells | shop
test: «The sandwich was dry until she added some mayo.» What does mayo mean here? | A cold drink | A county in Ireland | *A creamy sauce | A kind of bread
test: Which sentence is true about County Mayo? | It is a type of cheese | It is a sauce made from eggs | It is a mountain in Wales | *It is a county in the west of Ireland
exam: Read this: «Mayo is famous for its wild coast and Gaelic football.» What does Mayo mean here? | A sandwich | A creamy sauce | A type of cheese | *A county in Ireland
